.TH WB\-STATUS 1 "" "watchbill"
.SH NAME
wb\-status \- list the issues in the flow and where each stands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBwb\fR status [<issue>] [\-\-stage <heading>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
List the issues in the flow under headings, as git status lists files: each issue under the last step it has done (Not broken down, Broken down, Accepted, Tested, Built, Reviewed, Fixed), and last the issues that have a question no [answers] or [answer] line has closed. An issue is in the flow when its branch, local or at origin, holds a commit that the default branch of origin does not: git alone says which, and fetches nothing. Its line shows the branch, the open change as #<n> (change_of_branch) and how many commits are not pushed.
.PP
The comments come from issue_comments. <issue> prints that issue, in the flow or not, with its title (issue_address) and what it was worked out from; \-\-stage <heading> prints that heading only, whatever its case. For one issue it also prints a line kept: <role> round <n>, <k> commits not taken, <folder> for each view kept with work not taken back, and cut off: <role> round <n>, <folder> for each session whose wb ended before it did. With no issue it says on standard error how many such views are kept on this machine. Ends with 0 when every issue could be read, 1 when a pattern failed for one (it is listed under Not read), 2 when it was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.PP
Writes nothing but a temporary index in $TMPDIR, removed after, where it reads a kept view.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B <issue>
Print that issue, in the flow or not, with its title (issue_address) and what it was worked out from.
.TP
.B \-\-stage <heading>
Print that heading only, whatever its case.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every issue could be read.
.TP
.B 1
A pattern failed for one issue. It is listed under Not read.
.TP
.B 2
It was used wrongly or the repository is not set up.
.SH SEE ALSO
